                        ],
                        "form": "rewound"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78b2235f-65e0-38cb-9e15-eee8f478f030",
                        "entry_id": "4214dfe3-71e1-324b-82de-5f2ae8e667de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To wind (something) again."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c178c17b-682e-42ab-8478-3fcd1e638072",
                                "sense_id": "78b2235f-65e0-38cb-9e15-eee8f478f030",
                                "text": "A Myrish crossbowman poked his head out a different window, got off a bolt, and ducked down to rewind."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60c448f5-0139-415d-a1c8-76938b441d08",
                                "sense_id": "78b2235f-65e0-38cb-9e15-eee8f478f030",
                                "text": "[…] she was winding and rewinding bandages that were dripping in blood, smiling strangely at her as the plasma spilled from buckets all over the floor."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "51866e91-a24d-34ee-8bc9-0b26a1cb211f",
                        "entry_id": "4214dfe3-71e1-324b-82de-5f2ae8e667de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To wind (something) back, now especially of a cassette or a video tape, CD, DVD etc.; to go back on a video or audio recording."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "264266d3-bfe7-4652-8800-df8f706738a0",
                                "sense_id": "51866e91-a24d-34ee-8bc9-0b26a1cb211f",
                                "text": "If you need to reload film, the cassette can be rewound slightly by turning the hub located on one end of its spool."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3439ab01-5e9f-3c42-9f64-bdea01d783df",
                        "entry_id": "4214dfe3-71e1-324b-82de-5f2ae8e667de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To go back or think back to a previous moment or place, or a previous point in a discourse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7cb4c48-98d0-429e-84a9-99d5b5f3f1ec",
                                "sense_id": "3439ab01-5e9f-3c42-9f64-bdea01d783df",
                                "text": "If I had a time machine / And if life was a movie scene / I'd rewind, and I'd tell me / \"Ru-u-u-u-u-u-u-un\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "63da4713-57d2-4241-9c56-0bf6dfc102dc",
                                "sense_id": "3439ab01-5e9f-3c42-9f64-bdea01d783df",
                                "text": "To understand Russia, you have to dive deep into its history — boyars and czars, Pushkin and Pasternak, Stalin and Stalingrad. To understand the perils of underestimating Russia, you don't have to go back that far. Just rewind to 2001, when George W. Bush naively sized up Vladimir Putin as a leader he could work with, a conclusion Bush reached when he looked into the Russian leader's eyes and \"found him to be very straightforward and trustworthy."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c936c04-b100-4d32-8d59-c79db77be0ea",
                        "source_entry_id": "4214dfe3-71e1-324b-82de-5f2ae8e667de",
                        "source_sense_description": "to wind again",
                        "target_lang_word": "weer oprollen",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "42018c21-b1f1-4ef3-a505-ceff6c238e7a",
                        "source_entry_id": "4214dfe3-71e1-324b-82de-5f2ae8e667de",
                        "source_sense_description": "to wind again",
                        "target_lang_word": "rembobiner",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rembobiner",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "749e0dc9-1e43-3a53-9aad-a4759ddbdac0",
                                        "entry_id": "dae358ff-399d-3a37-bcb1-9ac6e94c1b16",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Embobiner de nouveau (quelque chose qui avait été débobiné)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5a71e86-9878-4651-b0b5-d1376cec86a8",
                                                "sense_id": "749e0dc9-1e43-3a53-9aad-a4759ddbdac0",
                                                "text": "Avant de rendre une cassette vidéo, il faut la rembobiner."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd3e77ab-c895-3849-8b0f-f86037efc5dd",
                                        "entry_id": "dae358ff-399d-3a37-bcb1-9ac6e94c1b16",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Faire un retour arrière sur une vidéo ou un morceau de musique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0d377b6-d95c-43d1-8396-d1d6f2be77f4",
                                                "sense_id": "bd3e77ab-c895-3849-8b0f-f86037efc5dd",
                                                "text": "Je n'ai pas bien compris le dialogue, tu pourrais rembobiner ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b76f1bd-d069-4f73-80f8-7a0343352b7d",
                                                "sense_id": "bd3e77ab-c895-3849-8b0f-f86037efc5dd",
                                                "text": "À la fin de leur chant, la bande se rembobinait et ils reprenaient du début. — (Daniel Nayeri, Duel à Toy Farm, dans Brigade des crimes imaginaires et autres histoires fantastiques et déglinguées, traduit de l’anglais par Valérie Le Plouhinec, Hélium, 2008, page 101)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60b7bf6e-b69f-433b-83a3-321e9e68faad",
                        "source_entry_id": "4214dfe3-71e1-324b-82de-5f2ae8e667de",
                        "source_sense_description": "to wind again",
                        "target_lang_word": "zurückspulen",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "zurückspulen",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c395e49f-e1f7-30ef-a65b-5c15437ac814",
                                        "entry_id": "eee37bb6-2cdb-3a4f-8289-774953034020",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ein auf einer Spule befindliches Band entgegen der Abspielrichtung wickeln (spulen) und so wieder zum Anfang gelangen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbf03321-b4dd-4ea2-851e-667a10baea1b",
                                                "sense_id": "c395e49f-e1f7-30ef-a65b-5c15437ac814",
                                                "text": "Bevor man das Video wieder in die Videothek brachte, hat man es zurückgespult."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e26cdb0f-9022-4af7-a9d9-8ea6391de7c6",
                                                "sense_id": "c395e49f-e1f7-30ef-a65b-5c15437ac814",
                                                "text": "Ach, spul doch noch mal zurück bis da, wo die Aufnahme von Hendrix kommt."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
